WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.571 --> 00:00:03.037
(alarm rings)
- Time to make the donuts.

00:00:03.037 --> 00:00:04.177
- [Narrator] "Dunkin'" has long said,

00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:06.180
"It's on time to make donuts."

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.830
- Who else goes to that trouble?

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.480
- But it's not just pastries.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.837
Over its 70 plus years

00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:13.650
"Dunkin'" has repeatedly
spotted and adapted

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.500
to new trends even when
that meant focusing less

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.700
on donuts.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.290
- Donuts literally used to be part

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.780
of their name and now it is not.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.210
And it definitely reflects how their sales

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.190
have really changed and how beverages

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.750
become so much more important

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.400
than just selling donuts.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.710
- [Narrator] From 2009 to 2019,

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.350
a time when Dunkin'
introduced many drink options

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.410
and rebranded, it grew from around 6,000

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.110
to over 9,000 locations.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.050
The shift away from donuts
and towards drinks is

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.540
just one change that has
helped the company evolve

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.150
from a New England diner
to a worldwide chain

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.653
worth around $9 billion.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.020
This is the economics of "Dunkin'".

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.930
In 1948 restaurateur, William Rosenberg

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.910
opened a diner called "Open Kettle"

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.220
in Quincy, Massachusetts selling coffee

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.740
for 10 cents and donuts for five.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.360
Two years later, he changed the name

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.070
to "Dunkin' Donuts" inspired

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.920
by seeing others dunk
donuts into their coffee.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.280
It was one of the first trends
the company capitalized on.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.720
- Donuts were actually served

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.760
to troops during the wars.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.110
- [Commentator] Behind the American lines

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.700
in Italy, a brief interlude

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.860
and good old fashioned donuts.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.500
- And when troops came home, it was 1950s

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.480
and people were going back to offices

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.780
and donuts were a really
great way to quickly

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.910
have breakfast on the go.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.130
And "Dunkin' Donuts"
really capitalize on that.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.080
- Dunkin' the magic munchkin.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.030
- [Narrator] The company
took donuts a step further

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.210
in the early 1970s when
they introduced the munchkin

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.920
as a way to use the leftover dough

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.330
from the center of donuts.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.884
- This is what a munchkin looks like.

00:01:47.884 --> 00:01:49.410
They have them down at "Dunkin' Donuts"

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.760
in quite a few flavors.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:51.690
- [Narrator] Donuts continued

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.940
to be Dunkin's focus through the nineties

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.100
when trends began to shift.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.940
In the 1990s, 2000s, America
was generally becoming

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:00.960
more health conscious.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.780
And donuts for all their tasty goodness

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.710
is not really known

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.590
as a very healthy breakfast alternative.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.380
So companies like "Dunkin'
Donuts" need to think

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.210
about what else could they serve.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.610
Meanwhile, "Starbucks" really was starting

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.430
to take on the US at that time

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.630
and was expanding a lot.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.030
And what they were doing
was inventing new kinds

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.260
of drinks.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.280
- [Narrator] Customers were looking

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.440
for caffeine and a lot of it.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.630
The number of US coffee houses doubled

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:30.540
between 1996 and 2001.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.850
So after decades of focusing on donuts,

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.770
in 2006, "Dunkin'" made one

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.150
of its first moves away

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.527
from the pastries when
it introduced the slogan,

00:02:38.527 --> 00:02:40.260
"America runs on Dunkin'".

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.060
Coffee and beverage sales were popular

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.440
for quick service restaurants

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.210
since they have better profit margins

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.043
than most offerings, like food.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.010
- When you think of a breakfast sandwich

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.680
or a baked good that involves labor,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.330
it often involves many different types

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.170
of ingredients.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.030
It might involve some kind of packaging,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.590
whereas coffee at its
simplest is just coffee

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.423
in a cup.

00:03:02.423 --> 00:03:03.600
The labor tends to be less

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.270
and that does make it
more profitable generally

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.470
for these drinks.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.390
- [Narrator] By 2011,
"Dunkin'" was selling

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.770
more hot and iced coffee

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.230
than any other fast food chain in the US,

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.850
including "Starbucks".

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.260
In New England and New York,

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.067
it hit 57% of the fast food coffee market.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:22.800
At the time, "Dunkin'"
had 6,800 locations,

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.930
around half the amount it has now

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.090
and bigger changes lay ahead.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:30.630
In 2018, Dunkin's rebrand
and name change to go

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.660
by just "Dunkin'" was a big step.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.790
That year, beverages made up 60%

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.110
of Dunkin's sales.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.280
- I think one of the important things

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.980
to recognize is caffeine is addictive

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.350
and everyone likes their morning coffee

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.150
and that is a ritual.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.300
So people often go to
get coffee every morning

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.710
where they might not necessarily

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.740
get a donut every morning
or some kind of food.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.390
- [Narrator] To give
customers more options

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.610
for their caffeine fix,
"Dunkin'" continued

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:59.460
to expand their drink
menu releasing espressos,

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.130
cappuccinos, lattes and Americanos.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.540
- [Artist] Take a sip
of "You've got this,"

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.040
with Dunkin' Espresso drinks.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.210
- [Narrator] And in doing so,

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.347
it went toe to toe with "Starbucks".

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:10.950
- "Dunkin'" is really trying to

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.500
in some ways get into Starbucks's lane.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:14.490
They've offered a lot

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.440
of different new kinds of beverages.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.220
They invested in machines
to offer espresso.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.950
They offer cold drinks,
they offer blended drinks

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.713
and they really are trying to,

00:04:24.713 --> 00:04:26.940
I would say, compete
more with "Starbucks",

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.950
whereas "Starbucks" probably still thinks

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.510
of itself as singular.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.280
- [Narrator] After the
push for more drink sales,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.930
in 2019, "Dunkin'" was one

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.250
of the top coffee sellers

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.990
of quick service restaurants selling

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.960
around 1.6 billion hot and iced coffees.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.370
In 2021, "Dunkin'" sold
over 4.4 billion cups.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.050
While caffeine is a big seller,

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.720
Dunkin's drink focus isn't just on drip.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.030
The company said that
highly visual beverages

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.770
are a focal point of its menu.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.690
They've also launched
more specialty drinks

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.430
like Matcha and Chai.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.650
Between all the flavors and coffee blends,

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.780
they've added nearly 50 new menu items

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.550
in the last four years.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.050
But on the food side of the menu,

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.000
the brand struggled during the pandemic

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.010
when the breakfast category was hit hard

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.950
by commuting changes caused by lockdowns.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.570
Dunkin's decline in sales would've

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.730
been nearly 5% points larger

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.890
if temporarily closed stores were included

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.030
in those numbers.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.340
But once again, hot and cold drinks

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.530
with their high profit margins continued

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.480
to be top sellers on the menu.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.430
- Earlier in the pandemic,

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.990
these cold drinks actually

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:31.845
were a real saving grace
for a lot of coffee chains,

00:05:31.845 --> 00:05:33.990
in part because people would order them

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:35.040
in the afternoon.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.560
It's really created a new day part

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.300
for them where they didn't have it before.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.010
And so that's been really helpful for them

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.930
when breakfast really took a hit early

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.250
in the pandemic.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.097
Around that time,

00:05:45.097 --> 00:05:47.430
"Dunkin'" was releasing new drinks.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:48.877
For example, in 2020

00:05:48.877 --> 00:05:50.340
"Dunkin'" announced the new--

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.720
- [Actor] Dunkin' Refresher.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.950
- [Narrator] And this summer they came out

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.540
with three iced pumpkin drinks

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.730
and a new flavor of refresher.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:00.360
- Cold drinks really have
exploded in popularity

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.130
including during the pandemic, and a lot

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.730
of it has to do with
social media, with TikTok.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.880
70% of sales for a lot of these chains now

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.380
is these cold beverages

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.750
which is a huge amount of growth

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:15.090
in a very short amount of time.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.290
- [Narrator] As beverages continue

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.520
to grow more popular,

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.070
Dunkin's experience in
developing buzzy drinks

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.357
may help it create more in the future.

00:06:22.357 --> 00:06:24.870
- "Dunkin'" certainly has
changed from the 1950s

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:25.710
when it was just known

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.530
as a coffee and donut company.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.150
They've expanded their drinks,

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.130
they've expanded their food

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.290
and thanks to franchising,

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.640
they've expanded their locations.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.290
So I do think they've evolved a lot

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.320
from their roots in Massachusetts.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:41.610
- [Narrator] As obstacles caused

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:42.810
by the pandemic continue

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.030
to challenge companies across the board,

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:46.860
it remains to be seen if Dunkin's history

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.723
of evolution will continue.

00:06:50.239 --> 00:06:52.822
(upbeat music)

